# R6 (ai/type-core-calculus.typ): two refinements of one stored value would
# give one dict two types. With deepCopy each refinement is its own dict, so
# writing a string through d cannot reach p.
"{\"age\": 1.5}" parseJson j!
@j deepCopy tryAs {age: float} ? p!
@j deepCopy tryAs {str: float | str} ? d!
@d "age" "x" set drop
@p :age? 1.0 + str wl
@d :age? str wl
